{"id":20,"flavor":[{"games":["Let’s Go, Eevee!","Let’s Go, Pikachu!","Yellow"],"text":"Its hind feet are webbed. They act as flippers, so it can swim in rivers and hunt for prey."},{"games":["Ultra Moon"],"text":"Its whiskers are essential for maintaining its balance. No matter how friendly you are, it will get angry and bite you if you touch its whiskers."},{"games":["Ultra Sun"],"text":"People say that it fled from its enemies by using its small webbed hind feet to swim from island to island in Alola."},{"games":["Moon"],"text":"Its disposition is far more violent than its looks would suggest. Don’t let your hand get too close to its face, as it could bite your hand clean off."},{"games":["Sun"],"text":"Its hind feet are webbed, so it’s a strong swimmer. It can cross rivers and sometimes even oceans."},{"games":["Alpha Sapphire","Omega Ruby","Sapphire","Ruby"],"text":"Raticate’s sturdy fangs grow steadily. To keep them ground down, it gnaws on rocks and logs. It may even chew on the walls of houses."},{"games":["Y","Crystal"],"text":"The webs on its hind legs enable it to cross rivers. It searches wide areas for food."},{"games":["X","White","Black","Platinum","Pearl","Diamond"],"text":"It whittles its constantly growing fangs by gnawing on hard things. It can chew apart cinder walls."},{"games":["White 2","Black 2"],"text":"With its long fangs, this surprisingly violent Pokémon can gnaw away even thick concrete with ease."},{"games":["SoulSilver","Silver"],"text":"Its whiskers help it to maintain balance. Its fangs never stop growing, so it gnaws to pare them down."},{"games":["HeartGold","Gold"],"text":"Gnaws on anything with its tough fangs. It can even topple concrete buildings by gnawing on them."},{"games":["LeafGreen","Blue","Red"],"text":"It uses its whiskers to maintain its balance. It apparently slows down if they are cut off."},{"games":["FireRed"],"text":"Its rear feet have three toes each. They are webbed, enabling it to swim across rivers."},{"games"